{"id":1326,"date":"2026-03-10T13:38:35","date_gmt":"2026-03-10T20:38:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?page_id=1326"},"modified":"2026-04-10T16:32:26","modified_gmt":"2026-04-10T23:32:26","slug":"cs280a-proj4","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/cs280a-proj4\/","title":{"rendered":"Neural Radiance Field"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Part 0: Calibrating Your Camera and Capturing a 3D Scan<\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\">.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Part 0.1: Calibrating My Camera<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To estimate the intrinsic parameters of my phone camera, I first captured 50 images of printed ArUco tags (4\u00d74 dictionary) from different viewpoints. The focal length was kept fixed (zoom = 1.0). <\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-7 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" data-attachment-id=\"997\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?attachment_id=997\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/IMG_5268.jpg?fit=800%2C600&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"800,600\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"IMG_5268\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uplo